# Per-model language z-scores on LTBv1 (Chinese-source subset)

Supporting data and replication script for:
"Accumulating Invisibility: How Platformised AI Translation Converts Cultural
Discount into a National-Image Externality" (submitted to Global Media and China).
The deposit is made under an anonymous creator name to preserve the journal's
double-anonymised review process.

## Contents

- `ltb_per_model_zscores.csv` — per-model within-language z-scores derived from the
  **Last Translation Benchmark (LTBv1)** Chinese-source items.
  Rows: 32 total = 31 machine-translation systems (7 China-developed, 24 non-China)
  plus 1 human baseline row (excluded from the model-level group comparison).
  Columns: `model`, `origin`, `zho_n` (number of Chinese-source cases scored),
  `within_model_z` (pass rate standardised within the model).
- `recompute_from_release.py` — self-contained replication script (standard library only).
  Reads only this CSV; no network access, no external dependencies.

## Reproduction

    python recompute_from_release.py

Expected output (matches the manuscript's reported values):

    CN-developed  : n=7, mean=1.3841, median=1.1851, positive=7/7
    Non-CN        : n=24, mean=0.0089, median=-0.1221, positive=9/24
    observed U    : 156.0
    exact two-sided p = 1.8710e-04   (two-sided exact Mann-Whitney U, no ties)
    ALL PASS

The z-score is standardised per model against that model's own pass-rate distribution;
it is a **capability-consistency diagnostic**, not a measure of ideological stance.
See manuscript SS4.2 and Proposition 4 (SS5.3).

## Upstream data

This package does **not** redistribute LTBv1. The underlying benchmark is available from:

- Zouhar, V. et al. (2026). The Last Translation Benchmark. arXiv:2609.04173.
- Dataset: https://huggingface.co/datasets/zouhar/last-translation-benchmark (CC BY 4.0)
- Code: https://github.com/zouharvi/last-translation-benchmark (MIT)

See `ATTRIBUTION.md`.
